context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"underspecified_oracle","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"underspecified_certification","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"medium","prod_impact":"low","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"self_revealing","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"medium"}}},{"block_threshold":0.7,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Resolve the capability assertion that 'unshare --map-root-user --mount' actually enforces filesystem write-denial (not merely that the binary is present): cite the util-linux/kernel version requirements for read-only bind-mount enforcement in a map-root-user namespace, and have the runtime probe verify enforcement (e.g., a write-denied smoke check) rather than binary presence alone.","cohort":["T1"],"criteria":["T1"],"decision":"block","decision_margin":0.2,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Plan text: 'Linux uses bwrap (bubblewrap) when present, else unshare --map-root-user --mount; the chosen mechanism is probed at runtime, not assumed.'","man7 mount_namespaces(7) (retrieved): 'it should not be possible to make the mount writable in a less privileged mount namespace' and the inverse read-only remount example returns 'mount: /mnt/dir: permission denied' under 'unshare --user --map-root-user --mount'","superuser.com (retrieved): rootless bind mount via unshare 'requires util-linux 2.39.1 which probably means ubuntu 23.04 or later'","The plan's probe verifies the mechanism is present but presence of the unshare binary does not establish that write-denial is actually enforced on the running kernel/util-linux version — the plan's own AC demands demonstrable DENY."],"finding":"The Linux second-choice fallback 'unshare --map-root-user --mount' is asserted to enforce filesystem write-denial, but this capability is unresolved: read-only bind-mount enforcement inside a map-root-user mount namespace is subject to kernel restrictions and util-linux version requirements, so the fallback may probe as 'present' yet not actually deny writes.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f9b76d2a63da203e4","impact":1.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Acceptance Criteria: 'Linux uses bwrap (bubblewrap) when present, else unshare --map-root-user --mount'","norm_id":"n18ff4697400cf2d3","priority":0.9,"reason":"high-priority+criterion-opted-in","recalled":false,"scenarios":["A contributor on a Linux host without bwrap but with an older util-linux: the probe selects unshare, reports it as the chosen mechanism, but the read-only bind mount does not stick and a mutated 'rm -rf' still lands — reproducing the incident under a sandbox believed active."],"severity":"critical","suggested_fix":"","tier":"LLM","validity":0.9,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"yes","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"no","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"yes","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"module","debt_impact":"medium","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"certification_cannot_prove","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"medium","prod_impact":"high","reversibility":"moderate","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"medium"}}},{"block_threshold":0.9,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Verify `unshare --map-root-user --mount` can create a write-restricting namespace unprivileged on the target Linux hosts (unprivileged-userns availability) and name the read-only-remount step that realizes the deny — or route to a SPIKE.","cohort":["T3"],"criteria":["T3"],"decision":"block","decision_margin":0.0,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Plan AC5: 'Linux uses `bwrap` (bubblewrap) when present, else `unshare --map-root-user --mount`.'","AC1 requires 'denying filesystem writes outside an explicit allow-list', but `unshare --mount` only isolates the mount namespace; a read-only remount step is unstated (Unverified capability on hosts with unprivileged userns disabled).","AC8 requires it 'works from a developer laptop with no CI involved' — the environment where unprivileged userns is most likely disabled."],"finding":"The plan asserts the Linux `unshare --map-root-user --mount` fallback denies filesystem writes outside an allow-list, but does not address that unprivileged user namespaces (CLONE_NEWUSER, required by `--map-root-user`) are disabled on many hardened Linux hosts, and that `unshare --mount` alone creates a private mount namespace without denying writes unless followed by a read-only remount. The flag set as stated is not sufficient to realize the write-deny, and the capability may be unavailable on a developer laptop.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f730d692737343e51","impact":1.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"AC5 (\"else `unshare --map-root-user --mount`\")","norm_id":"n9751f6ae4d76135b","priority":0.9,"reason":"high-priority+criterion-opted-in","recalled":false,"scenarios":["A developer laptop or CI runner with kernel.unprivileged_userns_clone=0 (or seccomp-restricted userns), where `unshare --map-root-user` fails and the fallback cannot enforce."],"severity":"critical","suggested_fix":"","tier":"LLM","validity":0.9,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"yes","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"no","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"yes","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"module","debt_impact":"medium","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"certification_cannot_prove","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"medium","prod_impact":"high","reversibility":"moderate","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"medium"}}},{"block_threshold":null,"blocking_enabled":null,"checklist_item":"","cohort":null,"criteria":["P6"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":null,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["2 criterion line(s) bundle multiple deliverables with 'and' (split so each is independently verifiable).","verify command `head` inspects output with `head` but asserts nothing — add an exit-code or comparison (-q, [ \"$(...)\" -eq N ], jq -e) so a failure is observable"],"finding":"Acceptance-criteria / definition-of-done quality issues.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f607dd457c67f9209","impact":0.4,"is_primary":null,"location":"","norm_id":"ned06ebc801a522e3","priority":0.4,"reason":null,"recalled":false,"scenarios":[],"severity":"minor","suggested_fix":"Split compound criteria, replace subjective terms with observable outcomes, and state how each is verified.","tier":"DET","validity":1.0,"verification":null},{"block_threshold":0.6,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Confirm the runtime sandbox and the static destructive-exec lint gate belong in one ticket (defense-in-depth for one incident) rather than two independently-releasable children, or state why they must land together.","cohort":["E3","E5","G5","T5b","T6","T9","necessity","project.portability"],"criteria":["G5"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.2229,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Sandbox ACs: 'Both shard-test-executing subprocesses in execute_shard() ... are wrapped in an OS-enforced sandbox'","Lint ACs: 'A lint gate flags a test that subprocess-execs a shell script containing an unguarded destructive deletion' and 'That gate runs in make lint'","DoD notes the sandbox lands in its own module while the lint gate is a separate script `check_destructive_test_exec.py` — two distinct deliverables"],"finding":"The ticket bundles two independently-releasable outcomes: (1) the OS-enforced sandbox wrapping both test-executing subprocesses (own module), and (2) a static lint gate flagging unguarded destructive subprocess-execs (own script `check_destructive_test_exec.py` + `make lint` wiring). Each is separately valuable, separately testable, and could ship on its own; they share only the 2026-08-26 incident as a root cause.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f8ea93fe2bbbd484d","impact":0.44,"is_primary":null,"location":"Acceptance Criteria (sandbox ACs 1-9) vs lint-gate ACs 10-11; Definition of Done","norm_id":"nf57dad8a55c7474a","priority":0.3771,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":[],"severity":"minor","suggested_fix":"","tier":"LLM","validity":0.8571,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"no","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"na","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"none","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"self_revealing","undecomposed":"bundles_separable_slices","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.9,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Verify against a current `man sandbox-exec` / live probe on the target macOS version that a generated write-deny Seatbelt profile still enforces (given Apple's deprecation of `sandbox-exec`), or route the macOS mechanism to a SPIKE before committing.","cohort":["T3"],"criteria":["T3"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.702,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Plan AC4: 'macOS uses Seatbelt `sandbox-exec` with a generated profile.'","sandbox-exec is a deprecated Apple CLI; deprecation status and continued enforcement on the target macOS version are not verified in the plan (Partially-verified: the tool exists but the specific enforcement surface on the target OS is unconfirmed)."],"finding":"The plan asserts macOS enforcement via `sandbox-exec` with a generated profile, but `sandbox-exec` is deprecated by Apple (emits a deprecation warning and is undocumented on recent macOS). Its continued write-deny enforcement on the target macOS version (macos-latest in CI) is a load-bearing external capability that the plan asserts without verifying against a current `man sandbox-exec` or a live probe.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fa4703430426d90f6","impact":0.264,"is_primary":null,"location":"AC4 (\"macOS uses Seatbelt sandbox-exec with a generated profile\") and Platform scope section","norm_id":"n40e0413b24051dae","priority":0.198,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["A future or current macos-latest image where sandbox-exec no longer enforces the profile, silently leaving the mutmut-run causal path unsandboxed."],"severity":"minor","suggested_fix":"","tier":"LLM","validity":0.75,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"insufficient","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"no","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"yes","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"module","debt_impact":"medium","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"high","reversibility":"moderate","silent_vs_self_revealing":"self_revealing","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"low"}}},{"block_threshold":0.9,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Name the concrete `bwrap` flags (e.g., --ro-bind /, --bind <scratch>, --bind <basetemp>, --bind <venv>, --dev-bind /dev/null) that realize the AC1 allow-list, verified against `bwrap --help`.","cohort":["T3"],"criteria":["T3"],"decision":"dropped","decision_margin":-0.801,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Plan AC5 names bwrap but no bwrap flags are enumerated anywhere in the plan.","AC1 describes the allow-list (scratch tree, pytest basetemp, venv, /dev/null) as a semantic goal, not as bwrap invocation flags (Partially-verified: bwrap exists and can do this, but the specific flag surface is unconfirmed)."],"finding":"The plan 